        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Clark McReynolds, Woodrow Wilson, John Calvin Coolidge Jr.\n- Roles: Republican lawyer, judge, United States Attorney General, Associate Justice of the United States Supreme Court, President of the United States\n\nFacts:\n- James Clark McReynolds was born on February 3, 1862, and died on August 24, 1946.\n- James Clark McReynolds was a Republican lawyer and judge.\n- James Clark McReynolds served as United States Attorney General under President Woodrow Wilson.\n- James Clark McReynolds served as an Associate Justice of the United States Supreme Court.\n- James Clark McReynolds served on the Supreme Court during the presidency of John Calvin Coolidge Jr., who was President of the United States from 1923 to 1929.",
